<title>HUNGARY: Csopak boosts op profit in 1996.</title>
<headline>Csopak boosts op profit in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ending December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of forints unless stated)</p>
<p>    Operating profit	    515.1	vs     354.4</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit		371.2	vs     392.8</p>
<p>    After-tax profit	    260.9	vs     290.2</p>
<p>    Net sales revenue	 8,612.5	vs   4,921.0</p>
<p>    Other revenue		 237.8	vs     148.9</p>
<p>    Material expenditures   6,842.3	vs   3,580.0</p>
<p>    Personnel expenditures    884.0	vs     691.2</p>
<p>    Depreciation		  125.5	vs	90.6</p>
<p>    Other costs		   322.7	vs     236.1</p>
<p>    Other expenditures	  257.0	vs     157.0</p>
<p>    Net financial income	 92.8 loss vs	47.2 profit</p>
<p>	Financial revenue	 146.6	vs     227.3</p>
<p>	Financial expenditures  239.5	vs     180.1</p>
<p>    Net extraordinary income   51.0 loss vs	 8.8 loss</p>
<p>	Extraordinary revenue   135.1	vs     355.9</p>
<p>	Extraordinary expend.   186.2	vs     364.7</p>
<p>    Taxation			111.4	vs     104.6</p>
<p>NOTE - Csopak Szovetkezeti Rt is a holding company, involved in trading, milling and cosmetics industries. The figures were calculated according to Hungarian Accounting Standards. The 1996 figures are not audited yet.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327-4040</p>
</text>
